   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">I’d like to fit a point process model where I have observations of a point process realization as well as some areal counts on partial areas <img src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/TbBcP_rYovhwwZogpPba1kMpsZLER3U7H0kXH49ns-mltiaZ-H2-qyogzewryEyn5a3B1R36exfsljzxNqlbCywuYIE=s0-d-e1-ft#https://chart.googleapis.com/chart?cht=tx&amp;chl=A_i\" alt=\"A_i\"> of the domain <img src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/y5wOmTLwm2zQB4t4dgYJ-Q5ZQW0vn1tSUTOP315UWLN48K2fKFXIBZt_RKkLgJfBuFk47ZwESFD_nfMzkR0_8f0x8wnrAkJa_A=s0-d-e1-ft#https://chart.googleapis.com/chart?cht=tx&amp;chl=%5COmega\" alt=\"\\Omega\">. That is, I have</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"><img src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/z1abOIxLZjprjoj7NcuPygpWxUN_9o36zuxi2cooNLN-cibbFEsbv3M4brJV2v-9bs-BmkIduUlaLbjh8OCnCp7ABsuiKl_sbYSF7QqrJIbgkxMBHRmnIjtYE-TOMcqGsJ36BIzfKYLFJAFqQYVKPNQN-ZMEMry57gwqHCvz=s0-d-e1-ft#https://chart.googleapis.com/chart?cht=tx&amp;chl=Z(s)%20%5Csim%20%5Coperatorname%7BMVN%7D(%5Cmu%2C%20%5CSigma)\" alt=\"Z(s) \\sim \\operatorname{MVN}(\\mu, \\Sigma)\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">where</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"><img src=\"https://ci4.googleusercontent.com/proxy/PlyqXaS638-vII2445J77L6F0RQm9bND6YQj3kPPOt_t6-2_pBwssV5LON-_bpbhfbYdPaZvsmUpPTw8Lq1Q4-tfRxCIsdIXTQ-F0PestV0WjQh_G3uKslFCS5zAJgHXdwIjnUvo13t28jBA=s0-d-e1-ft#https://chart.googleapis.com/chart?cht=tx&amp;chl=%5CLambda(s)%20%3D%20%5Cexp%5C%7BZ(s)%5C%7D\" alt=\"\\Lambda(s) = \\exp\\{Z(s)\\}\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">is the intensity field of the inhomogeneous Poisson process. I then have an observed point process. Following <a href=\"https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/spde-gitbook/ch-lcox.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/spde-gitbook/ch-lcox.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792442693771000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3EuQ9iB0sUCQsrscFkSFFE\">Chapter 4 of the SPDE book</a>, I can fit this with INLA.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">I would like to extend this to include additional observations of total counts within quadrats, of the form</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"><img src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/NCPrA6GqFtw2ZV5FMSRI6qHwajddvcGDblHKihrQzwTfmao0HCu9HMdqTNSxFHj_0Pf8ZLBZqJzT4Sfdylp7ujVhexAmDpImGWzm-ict-mUjMbJ1oDe06YLG08qb1XCm0zR46C6sbZYpRv-Nah_-_YuvSB8j8TphQKcYMhvEZ4HcQiXerlNKLV5kXEa1Utg7U8WPcZxYASPqAcfxqvWtOHC_Kp4VyXqpdK4L=s0-d-e1-ft#https://chart.googleapis.com/chart?cht=tx&amp;chl=y_i%20%5Csim%20%5Coperatorname%7BPoisson%7D%5Cleft(%5Cint_%7BA_i%7D%5C%20%5CLambda(s)%5C%20ds%5Cright)%2C\" alt=\"y_i \\sim \\operatorname{Poisson}\\left(\\int_{A_i}\\ \\Lambda(s)\\ ds\\right),\"></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">This isn’t linear in the predictor, as discussed in the <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/r-inla-discussion-group/change$20of$20support%7Csort:date/r-inla-discussion-group/TdATCDb6QUA/igfMrdhm9UYJ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!searchin/r-inla-discussion-group/change$20of$20support%257Csort:date/r-inla-discussion-group/TdATCDb6QUA/igfMrdhm9UYJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792442693772000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0gDlo2izX4XwaE82MyAY5g\">Spatial misalignment</a> discussion, so can’t be fit using INLA. But if I remember the ISEC workshop this past summer correctly, <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">inlabru</code> can deal with nonlinearities like this. Is it possible to define a likelihood that includes the change of support and the nonlinear transformation of the spatial field in <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">inlabru</code> to fit this model?</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Thanks,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">John Best</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdj5JJ2QgbGlrZSB0byBmaXQgYSBwb2ludCBwcm9jZXNzIG1vZGVsIHdoZXJlIEkgaGF2ZSBv\r\nYnNlcnZhdGlvbnMgb2YgYSBwb2ludCBwcm9jZXNzIHJlYWxpemF0aW9uIGFzIHdlbGwgYXMgc29t\r\nZSBhcmVhbCBjb3VudHMgb24gcGFydGlhbCBhcmVhcyAkQV9pJCBvZiB0aGUgZG9tYWluICRcT21l\r\nZ2EkLiBUaGF0IGlzLCBJIGhhdmU8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PiRaKHMpIFxzaW0g\r\nXG9wZXJhdG9ybmFtZXtNVk59KFxtdSwgXFNpZ21hKSQ8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2\r\nPndoZXJlPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj4kXExhbWJkYShzKSA9IFxleHBce1oocylc\r\nfSQ8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PmlzIHRoZSBpbnRlbnNpdHkgZmllbGQgb2YgdGhl\r\nIGluaG9tb2dlbmVvdXMgUG9pc3NvbiBwcm9jZXNzLiBJIHRoZW4gaGF2ZSBhbiBvYnNlcnZlZCBw\r\nb2ludCBwcm9jZXNzLiBGb2xsb3dpbmcgW0NoYXB0ZXIgNCBvZiB0aGUgU1BERSBib29rXShodHRw\r\nczovL2JlY2FyaW9wcmVjYXJpby5iaXRidWNrZXQuaW8vc3BkZS1naXRib29rL2NoLWxjb3guaHRt\r\nbCksIEkgY2FuIGZpdCB0aGlzIHdpdGggSU5MQS48L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pkkg\r\nd291bGQgbGlrZSB0byBleHRlbmQgdGhpcyB0byBpbmNsdWRlIGFkZGl0aW9uYWwgb2JzZXJ2YXRp\r\nb25zIG9mIHRvdGFsIGNvdW50cyB3aXRoaW4gcXVhZHJhdHMsIG9mIHRoZSBmb3JtPC9kaXY+PGRp\r\ndj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj4keV9pIFxzaW0gXG9wZXJhdG9ybmFtZXtQb2lzc29ufVxsZWZ0KFxp\r\nbnRfe0FfaX1cIFxMYW1iZGEocylcIGRzXHJpZ2h0KSwkPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRp\r\ndj5UaGlzIGlzbid0IGxpbmVhciBpbiB0aGUgcHJlZGljdG9yLCBhcyBkaXNjdXNzZWQgaW4gdGhl\r\nIFtTcGF0aWFsIG1pc2FsaWdubWVudF0oaHR0cHM6Ly9ncm91cHMuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbS9mb3J1bS8j\r\nIXNlYXJjaGluL3ItaW5sYS1kaXNjdXNzaW9uLWdyb3VwL2NoYW5nZSQyMG9mJDIwc3VwcG9ydCU3\r\nQ3NvcnQ6ZGF0ZS9yLWlubGEtZGlzY3Vzc2lvbi1ncm91cC9UZEFUQ0RiNlFVQS9pZ2ZNcmRobTlV\r\nWUopIG